            <ArticleTitle>[Qiantongding Decoction: An efficacious therapeutic for type III B prostatitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>89-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the clinical efficacy of Qiantongding Decoction in the treatment of type III B prostatitis or chronic pelvic pain syndrome (CPPS).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Seventy patients with type III B prostatitis / CPPS were randomly divided into an experimental group (n = 36) and a control group (n = 34), the former treated with Qiantongding Decoction, and the latter with oral Indometacin, both for a month. Then their scores on Pelvic Pain Symptom Survey and NIH-CPSI were documented and compared.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">An obvious improvement was observed in both groups after the treatment, with significant differences from pre-treatment (P &lt; 0.05), and the experimental group showed a significantly better alleviation of pain than the control (P &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Qiantongding Decoction has an obvious therapeutic effect on type III B prostatitis / CPPS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
